  "query_preview": "..\n\nAn upper-level ridge over the Four Corners region will result in\nfair weather this afternoon. However, the ridge will weaken \nthrough midweek as shortwave-induced minor perturbations \npropagate throughout the jet stream over Montana. Expect cooler \ntemperatures and increased cloud coverage tomorrow through \nThursday as a result.\n\nThe ridge will recover as the work week comes to a close. \nTemperatures will rebound as skies clear by Friday.\n\nFair conditions will not persist this weekend. The ridge will \nweaken and exit eastward ahead of an upper-level trough that will \ndig over Montana by Saturday morning. The trough will amplify as \nthe weekend progresses, with the associated low digging as far \nsouth as Oregon by Sunday. Subsequent strong cold air and moisture\nadvection will produce overcast skies, possible precipitation, \nand daily high temperatures in the 50s and 40s this weekend and \ninto Monday.\n\nPrecipitation chances this weekend are uncertain, but Saturday\nafternoon rain could potentially become snow Sunday and Monday as\ntemperatures dive. If snow occurs, ground accumulation is not\nlikely.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n- No changes from the NBM.\n\n- There is low confidence in precipitation type and amounts this\n  weekend.\n\n- There is high confidence in much cooler temperatures occuring\n  this weekend.\n\n\nDON",
